# @zteam

When this rule is attached (`@zteam`) or the user says **zteam** / **/zteam** / **@zteam/…**:

## Subcommands

| Trigger | Do this |
|---------|---------|
| **`@zteam/config`** | `get_zteam_config` → questions → `write_zteam_config` only (models source of truth). See `.zteam/README.MD`. |
| **`@zteam/documentation`** | `run_development_pipeline` with `workflow: "docs"`. |
| **`@zteam/tests`** | QA-focused pipeline (`fix` / `feature` / `resume` as appropriate). |
| **`@zteam`** (plain) | Full/auto pipeline as usual. |

## Always

1. Call MCP on **`user-zteam`** (not Cursor Task subagents).
2. Pass **`workspaceRoot`** = absolute Cursor-open folder (not sticky `mcp.json` `WORKSPACE_ROOT`).
3. Pass rich `userIdea` + **`projectRoot`** (prefer `samples/…`).
4. If `needsConfig`, run the config flow (or tell user `@zteam/config`) then re-run.
5. Report `workspaceRoot`, `appRoot`, `filesWritten`, `resumeHint`; never silently copy sibling projects.
